Installation on manjaro linux has proven to be basically easy by
reading the linux instructions and doing some simple follow-ups.

The main thing to solve is that manjaro is a distro that very closely
paces the qt versions of GoldenCheetah, but at the same time outpaces
it in regards to bison and other build infrastructure.

It has worked on both the Pinebook PRO and the Raspberry 4 for me. The
latter can be done with the Raspberry imager, hinted to a downloaded
manjaro for rasbpi, but it will basically just ignore WiFi setup
etc. from that tool.

After installation, these are some packages needed to compile
GoldenCheetah

- ssh, git
- g++ (I did not try yet CLANG)
- make, bison, flex, base-devel
- qt5-serialport, qt5-connectivity, qt5-charts, vlc, phonon-qt5-vlc,
- libusb

systemctl enable --now sshd # this might help
git clone git@github.com:nelbrecht/GoldenCheetah.git
cd GoldenCheetah && git checkout yaccfix
./local-build.sh

